# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .vercelignore — keep local secrets, data and artifacts out of CLI deployments.
#
# Vercel does NOT inherit .gitignore for `vercel deploy`: anything not listed
# here is uploaded with the deployment source, even if Git ignores it. An
# earlier deployment of this project shipped .env.vercel this way. Required
# source, migrations, assets and the env template are deliberately NOT excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real environment files (never upload). The template stays.
.env
.env*
!.env.example

# Local runtime data and project link state
.data/
.neon
.vercel/

# Dependencies and build output (rebuilt by Vercel)
node_modules/
.next/
out/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Tests, captures and coverage
test-results/
playwright-report/
e2e-results/
design-caps/
coverage/

# Editor / tool working directories
.zwork/
.zcode/

# Recordings and local deliverables (reports may contain private data)
*.mp4
*.webm
*.log
GitHub-Publish-Report.md
BUEL-Engineering-Work-Report.docx
